 A) Promise not to tell anyone and handle it yourself.
-B) Immediately get a supervisor/clinical lead, stay with the person if safe, share only what is needed for the safety assessment, follow the agency safety plan and relevant state law/case law — do not make solo disclosure decisions [M02-4][M02-8]. Note: This supervisor-involvement rule is for imminent-risk safety; it is not the same as KC 26 child-abuse reporting where statutory reporters must report immediately without prior approval/notification and then notify after [M02-5].
-C) Warn the other person directly yourself right away without supervisor.
